snapshot-menu (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Point every vendor-layer launcher at the per-tool wrapper path
    /opt/snapshot/<tool>/bin/<cmd> (with a matching TryExec), replacing the old
    /opt/snapshot/venv/bin and ad-hoc paths: opcua-client, uadiscover,
    pymodbus-console, plcscan, s7scan, ghidra, grassmarlin and firmware-mod-kit.
  * Add "ICS Python shell" (snapshot-ics-python.desktop) in Protocol Tools: a
    Python 3.11 shell with the ICS libraries on /opt/snapshot/ics-python.
  * Ship /etc/profile.d/snapshot-tools.sh and rewrite
    /etc/X11/Xsession.d/55snapshot-tools-path to APPEND the single wrapper dir
    /opt/snapshot/bin to PATH (so OS commands win); exec-in-shell appends it too
    instead of prepending the old venv/zeek dirs.

 -- Blackbird Cyber <snapshot@example.invalid>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

snapshot-menu (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Rework into a Kali-style menu: seven numbered engagement-phase folders
    (Recon, Traffic, Protocols, Firmware, Wireless, Reporting, Reference) at the
    top level, stock Xfce categories nested under "Usual Applications".
  * Divert libgarcon-common's root xfce-applications.menu so the layout applies
    to the panel menu, the Whisker menu and xfce4-appfinder; the seven folders
    merge in from applications-merged/snapshot.menu.
  * Pull the matching upstream GUI tools (Wireshark, PulseView, gqrx, GRC,
    CherryTree, Flameshot, KeePassXC, LibreOffice Writer) into their folders and
    exclude them from Usual Applications so they are not listed twice.
  * Replace the eight ad-hoc launchers with the full tool set; CLI tools run
    through usr/share/snapshot-menu/exec-in-shell so their output stays on
    screen, and vendor-layer tools carry TryExec so they hide when absent.
  * Ship /etc/X11/Xsession.d/55snapshot-tools-path so /opt/snapshot/venv/bin and
    /opt/snapshot/zeek/bin are on PATH for menu launchers.
  * Depend on desktop-file-utils.

 -- Blackbird Cyber <snapshot@example.invalid>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

